\function nhn-objectives-all() [[Målsetting]tagging[]] -[function[nhn-templates]]
\function nhn-objectives() [function[nhn-objectives-all]] -[function[nhn-archived]]
\function nhn-results() [[Resultat]tagging[]] -[function[nhn-excluded]]
\function nhn-service-group() [function[nhn-servicename]] :else[[(Uten tjeneste)]]
\function nhn-service-sortkey() [<currentTiddler>match[(Uten tjeneste)]then[ÿ]else<currentTiddler>]
\function nhn-objective-of() [<currentTiddler>tags[]] :filter[tag[Målsetting]] :else[[(Uten målsetting)]]
\function nhn-objective-sortkey() [<currentTiddler>match[(Uten målsetting)]then[ÿ]else<currentTiddler>]

Configuration for the delivery and OKR summaries (brief §3.4).

* `nhn-objectives` / `nhn-results` — the two OKR sets (`Målsetting`, `Resultat`); deliveries come from `nhn-deliveries`. `nhn-objectives-all` keeps archived objectives — the ToDo lists read it so archiving a year cannot falsify last year's status or blind copy detection.
* `nhn-service-group` — the service a delivery or OKR belongs to, via the service-name tag, falling back to `(Uten tjeneste)`. Roughly a quarter of deliveries and a third of results carry no service tag, so the fallback bucket is real and sorts last.
* `nhn-objective-of` — for a `Resultat`, the `Målsetting` it is tagged under (the parent↔child join is by tagging the parent's title). About one result in ten is unparented and falls into `(Uten målsetting)`.
* The `-sortkey` functions push those fallback buckets to the end of the list, matching `nhn-bu-sortkey` and `nhn-owner-sortkey`.

A tiddler tagged with two service names appears under both, so group counts can exceed the number of tiddlers in the set.
